  This file is covered by the Adam Runtime Exception
  (RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.md).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  System.Raven.Ext.adam - Raven (https://github.com/oscar-soirey/Raven, v0.3.0,
  Apache-2.0), a GUI library in C11 (widgets, layout panels, themes,
  XML-described windows, text input, menus, dialogs), as Adam objects over
  its C API. `import System.Raven.C, System.Raven.Ext;` builds user
  interfaces with it; the .C unit stays usable beside the objects.

  System.Raven.C is Raven's C API as cimport writes it from Raven.h (one
  unit for both targets), with the link libraries it needs per target:
  libraven.a (one per target, built by AdamLang-Libs' build-raven.cmd from
  Raven's own CMake project: static; examples, tests, tools and web pages
  off; shipped under Raven's Apache-2.0 license with its NOTICE and the
  licenses of the components it bundles in res\libs\vendor\licenses); on
  x86_64-windows-gnu winhttp user32 gdi32 shell32 comdlg32 ole32, on
  x86_64-linux-gnu X11 pthread m dl. Its Vulkan renderer opens the Vulkan
  loader at run time: nothing links it. This unit puts Raven's file loads
  on Adam's streams: it brings in System.HookIO (and through it the target
  triple's HookIO platform unit), whose hooks of the C runtime's file calls
  are what libraven.a's fopen / fread / fseek / ftell / fclose bind to.

  The object layer (every type starts `UI`, so nothing meets System.Raylib.Ext's):
  - Choices and sets: each of Raven's constant groups is a choices type
    with Raven's own values (`int32(UIKey.A)` is R_KEY_A, `UIKey(N)` the key
    Raven gave); a flag group is a set of a choices type whose value is the
    flag's bit number (R_WINDOW_HIDDEN = 2 is bit 1), so
    `int32(UIWindowFlags([UIWindowFlag.Hidden]))` is Raven's mask.
  - Value types: UIColor (float r, g, b, a: Raven runs on its own, so its
    colours are not raylib's bytes), UIPoint, UISize, UIRect, with methods
    and operators by `extend`; Raven's event and info records (REvent,
    RDropEvent ..) keep their .C names and fields and gain typed reads.
  - The app: `UIApp.Config()...Open()` (or `UIApp(name)`) opens Raven, the
    last UIApp copy ends it (every <Name>Res still alive destroyed first);
    `Run()` is a tool's loop, `Frame()` a game's. Raven's memory is Adam's
    heap while it runs, so a debug build's leak report counts it.
  - Handles, never owners: App and the objects Raven names are small
    values; what Raven gives the program to destroy is a <Name>Res, a
    shared handle the last copy destroys (UITimerRes ..).
  - Callbacks are closures: `On<Event>(func(..) begin .. end)`. Each Raven
    callback type has one clink trampoline here; its user_data is the key
    of the closure in that type's table, so a closure whose handle is gone
    is never reached. A closure set again releases the one before; a
    handle's closures go with it, the app's when the app ends.
  - Errors: UIErrors.Last, UIErrors.OnError(closure), UIErrors.Report()
    (console lines), the texts of codes and severities.
  - Widgets: UIWidget, a handle to a widget Raven owns and the base of
    every widget type; `Find<T>` / `As<T>` give a widget's typed view,
    checking its kind; a tree built in one chain (`Add`, `End()`), each
    child placed by a UILayout; events as closures, released when Raven
    destroys the widget (its OnDestroy run then).
  - Windows: UIWindow, a handle to a top-level window (UIWindowConfig opens
    one in a chain): its content, look, state, input, popups, dialogs and
    message boxes, its events as closures; UITouch (the app's touch and
    pen settings) and UIDrag (the app's own drag and drop).
  - Widget types (V4): the layout containers (UIVBox, UIHBox, UIGrid ..
    UITabView, UIExpander) and the controls (UILabel, UIButton ..
    UIColorPicker, UIToast), each `object(UIWidget)` with its own
    `Create` and `Kinds`; their members join UIWidget's of the same name
    as overloads; `Begin<T>()` opens a child container in a chain.
  - Lists (V5): UIListView, UITreeView (UITreeItem), UITable (UITableColumn,
    UITableRow), UITileView (UITileSection; tiles described in UITile /
    UITileHeader records), UIMenuBar / UIMenu / UIMenuItem; the texts a
    virtual list's closure hands Raven held until its next call.
  - Editors and views (V6): UITextEditor (UITextPos / UITextSpan places,
    undo, colouring by language, completion, markers, hover tooltips),
    UIFileBrowser (UIFileFilter), UIViewport (the app's own renderer),
    UICustom (painted through a UIPainter in its paint closure) and
    UICarousel.
  - Charts, documents and maps (V7): UIPlot (UIPlotSeries, UIPlotAxis,
    UIDragLine), UIChart (pie / donut UIChartSlice, gauge, heatmap,
    sparkline), UIPDFView, UIMapView (UIMapMarker; tiles the program
    hands it) and UIPDFDocRes (a PDF the program writes, UIPrintDesc).
  - Tools and shell (V8): UITimeline (UITrack, UITimelineItem), UINodeGraph
    (UIGraphNode, UIGraphPin, UIGraphLink), UIBlockEditor (UIBlock),
    UIDockArea (UIDockPanel), UIIsland (a window's own: UIWindow.Island),
    UIHeaderBar and UIBackgroundBlur.
  - Resources and the theme (V9): UITextureRes, UIFontRes, UIShaderRes
    (shared handles; what shows one keeps a copy), UIPixels and UITheme.
  - Actions and system UI (V9): UIActions (+ UIActionContext), UILocale,
    UIAccessibility, UIScript, UISyntaxLanguage (UILanguageDef),
    UIFileDialog, UITrayRes and UIFiles.
  - XML (V10): UIXML (paths, auto-loading, live reload, declared tags and
    tags made by code), UIXMLDocRes (a document read, changed, built and
    written back) and UIXMLNode (UIWidget.XMLNode: the node it came from).
  - Hosting (V10): UIHost (+ UIHostPlatform: Raven in another program's
    windows, its input injected, a backend of the program's own) and
    UIVulkan (Raven's Vulkan device shared with an engine).

  Inside a raylib program Raven is used through System.Raven.Raylib's
  RaylibHost
  (raylib keeps the window, the loop, audio and the game's drawing; Raven
  draws its widgets in the raylib frame). Raven's C API itself:
  - Setup: Rinit(R_BACKEND_VULKAN) opens Raven with its own OS windows;
    Rinit_ex(addr of LDesc) takes an RInitDesc (backend, app_name,
    headless = R_TRUE for no OS window, disable_render_thread).
    R_BACKEND_NULL renders nothing (headless runs and tests). Rshutdown()
    ends it.
  - Windows and widgets: Rwindow_create(title, width, height,
    R_WINDOW_DEFAULT) gives a window's Rid; Rwidget_create(R_WIDGET_VBOX)
    and the kind constructors (Rlabel_create, Rbutton_create, ...) give
    widgets; Rwidget_add_child(parent, child) places a child and returns
    it; Rwindow_set_content(window, root) sets what a window shows.
  - Each frame: Rdraw_frame() processes the pending events, runs the
    posted tasks and timers, then lays out and paints the windows that
    changed (0 once Rquit was called or the last window is closed); a
    headless window takes its input through Rwindow_inject_mouse_move /
    _mouse_button / _mouse_wheel / _key / _text.
  - Text: Raven's ptr to const char results (Rlabel_get_text,
    Rclipboard_get_text, ...) are Raven's memory; StringFromC
    (System.SysUtils) copies one into an Adam string.
  - Device loss: when the GPU device is lost, Raven makes a new one at the
    next frame and remakes its surfaces, textures and shaders; the
    application rebuilds what it made itself in UIApp.OnDeviceReset (on
    the UI thread during a frame). A custom backend reports the loss with
    Rbackend_device_lost() (thread-safe, from the render thread);
    Rvulkan_simulate_device_lost() acts as if the Vulkan device was lost,
    to test the recovery (nothing with an external device).
  - Texture filters: Rtexture_set_filter(texture, filter) takes
    R_FILTER_LINEAR, R_FILTER_NEAREST (pixel art) or R_FILTER_MIPMAP
    (smooth with mipmaps, for images shown much smaller than their size).
    Textures made from image files start with R_FILTER_MIPMAP, the others
    with R_FILTER_LINEAR. A backend without mipmaps treats MIPMAP as
    LINEAR: System.Raven.Raylib draws every filter but NEAREST as raylib's
    LINEAR.
  - Timeline sizes: Rtimeline_set_header_width (the track-name column),
    Rtimeline_set_ruler_height and Rtimeline_set_default_track_height, each
    in logical units with 0 for the automatic size, and their
    Rtimeline_get_ forms (get_header_width returns the width as laid out).
  - Files: every load (XML windows, themes, fonts, textures, Rfile_read)
    looks in Raven's memory files first (Rfile_register_memory), then opens
    the path with the C runtime, which this unit's HookIO reaches: a zip
    such as bin\assets.zip loads with Raven's own calls, through an io://
    prefix (System.HookIO's RegisterIOSource(CreateZipIOSource(archive,
    password)) + "/entry") or with the zip as the thread's path source
    (SetIOThreadPathSource) and the entry's own name. An XML window's
    images and fonts are named relative to it and come from the same
    place.

  The unit names no OS: the hooks the C runtime's names bind to are the
  HookIO platform unit's that the target triple picks.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit System.Raven.Ext;

// System.HookIO imports the triple's HookIO platform unit: its hooks are the
// C runtime's file names libraven.a's loads bind to
import System.SysUtils, System.Collections, System.CustomIO, System.HookIO, System.Raven.C;

// ============================================================================
// Choices and sets (listing sec 1), every value Raven's own constant's
// (written by scripts\ravenapi\gen_ui_choices.py from System.Raven.C).
// ============================================================================

public type
  /// The renderer Raven draws with (`R_BACKEND_*`): `Null` renders nothing (headless runs, tests).
  UIBackend = choices(
    Default = 0,  /// The renderer of the platform: WebGL in browser builds, Metal on macOS and iOS when it is compiled, Vulkan otherwise. C: R_BACKEND_DEFAULT
    Vulkan,       /// Built-in Vulkan renderer. C: R_BACKEND_VULKAN
    Null,         /// Renders nothing. Used for headless runs and unit tests. C: R_BACKEND_NULL
    Custom,       /// Backend supplied with Rbackend_register (see raven_backend.h). C: R_BACKEND_CUSTOM
    WebGL,        /// Browser renderer (Emscripten, WebGL 2). C: R_BACKEND_WEBGL
    Metal);       /// Built-in Metal renderer (macOS, iOS). C: R_BACKEND_METAL

  /// An error Raven reports (`R_NO_ERROR`, `R_ERROR_*`).
  UIErrorCode = choices(
    None = 112,         /// No error. C: R_NO_ERROR
    InvalidId,          /// The invalid id error. C: R_ERROR_INVALID_ID
    InvalidEnum,        /// The invalid enum error. C: R_ERROR_INVALID_ENUM
    InvalidValue,       /// The invalid value error. C: R_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE
    InvalidOperation,   /// The invalid operation error. C: R_ERROR_INVALID_OPERATION
    Backend,            /// The backend error. C: R_ERROR_BACKEND
    Platform,           /// The platform error. C: R_ERROR_PLATFORM
    OutOfMemory,        /// The out of memory error. C: R_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY
    InvalidFileFormat,  /// The invalid file format error. C: R_ERROR_INVALID_FILE_FORMAT
    FileNotFound,       /// The file not found error. C: R_ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND
    XML,                /// The XML error. C: R_ERROR_XML
    WrongThread,        /// The wrong thread error. C: R_ERROR_WRONG_THREAD
    Script);            /// A diagnostic of Raven Script (raven_script.h): the text is the whole message, "error[RS102]: ...". C: R_ERROR_SCRIPT

  /// How bad a reported error is (`R_SEVERITY_*`).
  UISeverity = choices(
    WeakWarning = 128,  /// Weak warning. C: R_SEVERITY_WEAK_WARNING
    Warning,            /// Warning. C: R_SEVERITY_WARNING
    Error,              /// Error. C: R_SEVERITY_ERROR
    Fatal);             /// Fatal. C: R_SEVERITY_FATAL

  /// A life-cycle event of the application (`R_APP_*`).
  UIAppEvent = choices(
    WillPause = 2944,  /// The application is about to leave the front (home, app switcher, a call). Save the state now. C: R_APP_WILL_PAUSE
    DidPause,          /// The application is in the background: Raven has stopped drawing, and waited until the GPU was idle. C: R_APP_DID_PAUSE
    WillResume,        /// The application is coming back to the front: Raven draws again. C: R_APP_WILL_RESUME
    DidResume,         /// The application is in front and takes input again. C: R_APP_DID_RESUME
    LowMemory,         /// The system is low on memory: free what can be made again. Raven then drops its own caches and trims its heap. C: R_APP_LOW_MEMORY
    WillTerminate);    /// The application is about to end (Android: the activity is finishing; its window is closed right after). C: R_APP_WILL_TERMINATE

  /// A window's creation flag (`R_WINDOW_*`; none is Raven's `R_WINDOW_DEFAULT`).
  /// A member's value is its bit number in Raven's flags (a set of them casts to them).
  UIWindowFlag = choices(
    NoResize = 0,   /// The user cannot resize it. C: R_WINDOW_NO_RESIZE
    Hidden,         /// Made hidden. C: R_WINDOW_HIDDEN
    Borderless,     /// No system frame or title bar. C: R_WINDOW_BORDERLESS
    Maximized,      /// Made maximized. C: R_WINDOW_MAXIMIZED
    CustomHeader,   /// No title bar from the OS: the content covers the whole window and draws its own header, with a R_WIDGET_HEADER_BAR (raven_shell.h) or with any widget given to Rwidget_set_window_drag. The window is still moved, resized, snapped and maximized by the OS, as it does for its own title bars. C: R_WINDOW_CUSTOM_HEADER
    Transparent,    /// The window can be seen through: where the application draws nothing opaque, what is behind the window on the screen shows (the desktop, the other applications), not a color of the application. Glass then looks at the screen itself. What the OS does to what shows through is chosen with Rwindow_set_backdrop. See RBackdrop for what each window system can do. C: R_WINDOW_TRANSPARENT
    SplashScreen);  /// A splash screen: shown while the application starts. No frame (it implies R_WINDOW_BORDERLESS and R_WINDOW_NO_RESIZE, and cancels R_WINDOW_MAXIMIZED and R_WINDOW_CUSTOM_HEADER), centered on the screen before it is first shown and again when its size changes, above the other windows, out of the taskbar and of Alt+Tab (Windows), of the Window menu and of Cmd+` (macOS), typed _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_SPLASH on X11. Wayland gives it no place of its own: it is a window without frame there. The application destroys it once its main window is ready (creating the main window first keeps Ris_running true). C: R_WINDOW_SPLASH_SCREEN
  /// A set of `UIWindowFlag` (Raven's `RWindowFlags`).
  UIWindowFlags = set of UIWindowFlag;

  /// The OS windowing system a window runs on (`R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_*`).
  UIWindowSystem = choices(
    None = 144,  /// None. C: R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_NONE
    Win32,       /// Win32. C: R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_WIN32
    X11,         /// X11. C: R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_X11
    Wayland,     /// Wayland. C: R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_WAYLAND
    Cocoa,       /// Cocoa (macOS). C: R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_COCOA
    Emscripten,  /// Emscripten. C: R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_EMSCRIPTEN
    Android,     /// Android. C: R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_ANDROID
    UIKit);      /// UIKit (iOS). C: R_WINDOW_SYSTEM_UIKIT

  /// The screen corner a picture-in-picture window sits in (`R_PIP_*`).
  UIPipCorner = choices(
    BottomRight = 1920,  /// The bottom right corner. C: R_PIP_BOTTOM_RIGHT
    BottomLeft,          /// The bottom left corner. C: R_PIP_BOTTOM_LEFT
    TopRight,            /// The top right corner. C: R_PIP_TOP_RIGHT
    TopLeft);            /// The top left corner. C: R_PIP_TOP_LEFT

  /// What shows behind a window (`R_BACKDROP_*`).
  UIBackdrop = choices(
    None = 1024,  /// Opaque: the window color, or the wallpaper of the theme. C: R_BACKDROP_NONE
    Transparent,  /// The screen behind the window, as it is. C: R_BACKDROP_TRANSPARENT
    Blur,         /// The screen behind the window, blurred by the OS. C: R_BACKDROP_BLUR
    Acrylic,      /// Blurred, tinted and grained by the OS (the acrylic of Windows). C: R_BACKDROP_ACRYLIC
    Mica);        /// A soft tint taken from the wallpaper of the desktop (the mica of Windows 11). C: R_BACKDROP_MICA

  /// The kind of text a text input takes, for on-screen keyboards (`R_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_*`).
  UIInputType = choices(
    Text = 2912,  /// Plain text. C: R_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_TEXT
    Email,        /// An email address. C: R_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_EMAIL
    Number,       /// Digits. C: R_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_NUMBER
    Decimal,      /// Digits and a decimal separator. C: R_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_DECIMAL
    Phone,        /// A phone number. C: R_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_PHONE
    URL,          /// A URL. C: R_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_URL
    Search);      /// A search. C: R_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_SEARCH

  /// How text lines up in its box (`R_TEXT_ALIGN_*`).
  UITextAlign = choices(
    Left = 640,  /// Lined up on the left. C: R_TEXT_ALIGN_LEFT
    Center,      /// Centred. C: R_TEXT_ALIGN_CENTER
    Right);      /// Lined up on the right. C: R_TEXT_ALIGN_RIGHT

  /// The label of an on-screen keyboard's return key (`R_RETURN_KEY_*`).
  UIReturnKey = choices(
    Default = 2928,  /// The system's own label. C: R_RETURN_KEY_DEFAULT
    Done,            /// The return key reads "Done". C: R_RETURN_KEY_DONE
    Go,              /// The return key reads "Go". C: R_RETURN_KEY_GO
    Next,            /// The return key reads "Next". C: R_RETURN_KEY_NEXT
    Search,          /// The return key reads "Search". C: R_RETURN_KEY_SEARCH
    Send);           /// The return key reads "Send". C: R_RETURN_KEY_SEND

  /// A window edge or corner, for resizing (`R_EDGE_*`).
  UIEdge = choices(
    Left = 208,    /// The left edge. C: R_EDGE_LEFT
    Right,         /// The right edge. C: R_EDGE_RIGHT
    Top,           /// The top edge. C: R_EDGE_TOP
    Bottom,        /// The bottom edge. C: R_EDGE_BOTTOM
    TopLeft,       /// The top-left corner. C: R_EDGE_TOP_LEFT
    TopRight,      /// The top-right corner. C: R_EDGE_TOP_RIGHT
    BottomLeft,    /// The bottom-left corner. C: R_EDGE_BOTTOM_LEFT
    BottomRight);  /// The bottom-right corner. C: R_EDGE_BOTTOM_RIGHT

  /// A mouse button (`R_MOUSE_*`).
  UIPointerButton = choices(
    Left = 0,  /// The left mouse button. C: R_MOUSE_LEFT
    Right,     /// The right mouse button. C: R_MOUSE_RIGHT
    Middle,    /// The middle mouse button. C: R_MOUSE_MIDDLE
    X1,        /// The X1 mouse button. C: R_MOUSE_X1
    X2);       /// The X2 mouse button. C: R_MOUSE_X2

  /// A modifier key held with an input (`R_MOD_*`).
  /// A member's value is its bit number in Raven's flags (a set of them casts to them).
  UIModifier = choices(
    Shift = 0,  /// The Shift key. C: R_MOD_SHIFT
    Ctrl,       /// The Ctrl key. C: R_MOD_CTRL
    Alt,        /// The Alt key. C: R_MOD_ALT
    Super);     /// The Super key. C: R_MOD_SUPER
  /// A set of `UIModifier` (Raven's `RModifier`).
  UIModifiers = set of UIModifier;

  /// A mouse cursor shape (`R_CURSOR_*`).
  UICursor = choices(
    Arrow = 176,  /// The arrow cursor. C: R_CURSOR_ARROW
    IBeam,        /// The I-beam (text) cursor. C: R_CURSOR_IBEAM
    Hand,         /// The hand cursor. C: R_CURSOR_HAND
    Crosshair,    /// The crosshair cursor. C: R_CURSOR_CROSSHAIR
    ResizeH,      /// The left-right resize cursor. C: R_CURSOR_RESIZE_H
    ResizeV,      /// The up-down resize cursor. C: R_CURSOR_RESIZE_V
    ResizeNWSE,   /// The top-left to bottom-right resize cursor. C: R_CURSOR_RESIZE_NWSE
    ResizeNESW,   /// The top-right to bottom-left resize cursor. C: R_CURSOR_RESIZE_NESW
    Move,         /// The move cursor. C: R_CURSOR_MOVE
    NotAllowed,   /// The not allowed cursor. C: R_CURSOR_NOT_ALLOWED
    None);        /// No pointer at all (a game that hides it). Windows; elsewhere the arrow. C: R_CURSOR_NONE

  /// A keyboard key (`R_KEY_*`; the digit keys `Key0` .. `Key9`).
  UIKey = choices(
    Unknown = 0,      /// The unknown key. C: R_KEY_UNKNOWN
    Space = 32,       /// The space key. C: R_KEY_SPACE
    Apostrophe = 39,  /// The apostrophe key. C: R_KEY_APOSTROPHE
    Comma = 44,       /// The comma key. C: R_KEY_COMMA
    Minus,            /// The minus key. C: R_KEY_MINUS
    Period,           /// The period key. C: R_KEY_PERIOD
    Slash,            /// The slash key. C: R_KEY_SLASH
    Key0,             /// The 0 key. C: R_KEY_0
    Key1,             /// The 1 key. C: R_KEY_1
    Key2,             /// The 2 key. C: R_KEY_2
    Key3,             /// The 3 key. C: R_KEY_3
    Key4,             /// The 4 key. C: R_KEY_4
    Key5,             /// The 5 key. C: R_KEY_5
    Key6,             /// The 6 key. C: R_KEY_6
    Key7,             /// The 7 key. C: R_KEY_7
    Key8,             /// The 8 key. C: R_KEY_8
    Key9,             /// The 9 key. C: R_KEY_9
    Semicolon = 59,   /// The semicolon key. C: R_KEY_SEMICOLON
    Equal = 61,       /// The equal key. C: R_KEY_EQUAL
    A = 65,           /// The A key. C: R_KEY_A
    B,                /// The B key. C: R_KEY_B
    C,                /// The C key. C: R_KEY_C
    D,                /// The D key. C: R_KEY_D
    E,                /// The E key. C: R_KEY_E
    F,                /// The F key. C: R_KEY_F
    G,                /// The G key. C: R_KEY_G
    H,                /// The H key. C: R_KEY_H
    I,                /// The I key. C: R_KEY_I
    J,                /// The J key. C: R_KEY_J
    K,                /// The K key. C: R_KEY_K
    L,                /// The L key. C: R_KEY_L
    M,                /// The M key. C: R_KEY_M
    N,                /// The N key. C: R_KEY_N
    O,                /// The O key. C: R_KEY_O
    P,                /// The P key. C: R_KEY_P
    Q,                /// The Q key. C: R_KEY_Q
    R,                /// The R key. C: R_KEY_R
    S,                /// The S key. C: R_KEY_S
    T,                /// The T key. C: R_KEY_T
    U,                /// The U key. C: R_KEY_U
    V,                /// The V key. C: R_KEY_V
    W,                /// The W key. C: R_KEY_W
    X,                /// The X key. C: R_KEY_X
    Y,                /// The Y key. C: R_KEY_Y
    Z,                /// The Z key. C: R_KEY_Z
    LeftBracket,      /// The left bracket key. C: R_KEY_LEFT_BRACKET
    Backslash,        /// The backslash key. C: R_KEY_BACKSLASH
    RightBracket,     /// The right bracket key. C: R_KEY_RIGHT_BRACKET
    Grave = 96,       /// The grave key. C: R_KEY_GRAVE
    Escape = 256,     /// The escape key. C: R_KEY_ESCAPE
    Enter,            /// The enter key. C: R_KEY_ENTER
    Tab,              /// The tab key. C: R_KEY_TAB
    Backspace,        /// The backspace key. C: R_KEY_BACKSPACE
    Insert,           /// The insert key. C: R_KEY_INSERT
    Delete,           /// The delete key. C: R_KEY_DELETE
    Right,            /// The right key. C: R_KEY_RIGHT
    Left,             /// The left key. C: R_KEY_LEFT
    Down,             /// The down key. C: R_KEY_DOWN
    Up,               /// The up key. C: R_KEY_UP
    PageUp,           /// The page up key. C: R_KEY_PAGE_UP
    PageDown,         /// The page down key. C: R_KEY_PAGE_DOWN
    Home,             /// The home key. C: R_KEY_HOME
    End,              /// The end key. C: R_KEY_END
    CapsLock,         /// The caps lock key. C: R_KEY_CAPS_LOCK
    PrintScreen,      /// The print screen key. C: R_KEY_PRINT_SCREEN
    Pause,            /// The pause key. C: R_KEY_PAUSE
    F1,               /// The F1 key. C: R_KEY_F1
    F2,               /// The F2 key. C: R_KEY_F2
    F3,               /// The F3 key. C: R_KEY_F3
    F4,               /// The F4 key. C: R_KEY_F4
    F5,               /// The F5 key. C: R_KEY_F5
    F6,               /// The F6 key. C: R_KEY_F6
    F7,               /// The F7 key. C: R_KEY_F7
    F8,               /// The F8 key. C: R_KEY_F8
    F9,               /// The F9 key. C: R_KEY_F9
    F10,              /// The F10 key. C: R_KEY_F10
    F11,              /// The F11 key. C: R_KEY_F11
    F12,              /// The F12 key. C: R_KEY_F12
    Kp0,              /// The keypad 0 key. C: R_KEY_KP_0
    Kp1,              /// The keypad 1 key. C: R_KEY_KP_1
    Kp2,              /// The keypad 2 key. C: R_KEY_KP_2
    Kp3,              /// The keypad 3 key. C: R_KEY_KP_3
    Kp4,              /// The keypad 4 key. C: R_KEY_KP_4
    Kp5,              /// The keypad 5 key. C: R_KEY_KP_5
    Kp6,              /// The keypad 6 key. C: R_KEY_KP_6
    Kp7,              /// The keypad 7 key. C: R_KEY_KP_7
    Kp8,              /// The keypad 8 key. C: R_KEY_KP_8
    Kp9,              /// The keypad 9 key. C: R_KEY_KP_9
    KpDecimal,        /// The keypad decimal key. C: R_KEY_KP_DECIMAL
    KpDivide,         /// The keypad divide key. C: R_KEY_KP_DIVIDE
    KpMultiply,       /// The keypad multiply key. C: R_KEY_KP_MULTIPLY
    KpSubtract,       /// The keypad subtract key. C: R_KEY_KP_SUBTRACT
    KpAdd,            /// The keypad add key. C: R_KEY_KP_ADD
    KpEnter,          /// The keypad enter key. C: R_KEY_KP_ENTER
    LeftShift,        /// The left shift key. C: R_KEY_LEFT_SHIFT
    LeftCtrl,         /// The left Ctrl key. C: R_KEY_LEFT_CTRL
    LeftAlt,          /// The left alt key. C: R_KEY_LEFT_ALT
    LeftSuper,        /// The left super key. C: R_KEY_LEFT_SUPER
    RightShift,       /// The right shift key. C: R_KEY_RIGHT_SHIFT
    RightCtrl,        /// The right Ctrl key. C: R_KEY_RIGHT_CTRL
    RightAlt,         /// The right alt key. C: R_KEY_RIGHT_ALT
    RightSuper,       /// The right super key. C: R_KEY_RIGHT_SUPER
    Menu);            /// The menu key. C: R_KEY_MENU

  /// The kind of a widget input event (`R_EVENT_*`).
  UIEventKind = choices(
    None = 192,   /// No event. C: R_EVENT_NONE
    MouseMove,    /// A mouse move event. C: R_EVENT_MOUSE_MOVE
    MouseDown,    /// A mouse down event. C: R_EVENT_MOUSE_DOWN
    MouseUp,      /// A mouse up event. C: R_EVENT_MOUSE_UP
    MouseWheel,   /// A mouse wheel event. C: R_EVENT_MOUSE_WHEEL
    MouseEnter,   /// A mouse enter event. C: R_EVENT_MOUSE_ENTER
    MouseLeave,   /// A mouse leave event. C: R_EVENT_MOUSE_LEAVE
    KeyDown,      /// A key down event. C: R_EVENT_KEY_DOWN
    KeyUp,        /// A key up event. C: R_EVENT_KEY_UP
    Text,         /// A character was typed. `codepoint` holds the Unicode scalar value. C: R_EVENT_TEXT
    FocusGained,  /// A focus gained event. C: R_EVENT_FOCUS_GAINED
    FocusLost);   /// A focus lost event. C: R_EVENT_FOCUS_LOST

  /// The stage of a drag and drop over a widget (`R_DROP_*`).
  UIDropPhase = choices(
    Enter = 224,  /// The pointer came over the target. C: R_DROP_ENTER
    Move,         /// It moves over the target. C: R_DROP_MOVE
    Leave,        /// It left the target without dropping. C: R_DROP_LEAVE
    Dropped);     /// The user dropped: `paths` and `text` hold what was dropped. C: R_DROP_DROPPED

  /// How a widget takes touch input (`R_TOUCH_MODE_*`).
  UITouchMode = choices(
    Auto = 1152,  /// The finger scrolls what scrolls under it, and is a mouse elsewhere (default). C: R_TOUCH_MODE_AUTO
    Scroll,       /// A finger moving on the widget always scrolls what contains it, even over a control that drags. C: R_TOUCH_MODE_SCROLL
    Mouse,        /// The finger is a mouse on the widget: pressing presses at once, moving drags, nothing scrolls. C: R_TOUCH_MODE_MOUSE
    None);        /// Fingers are ignored on the widget (only its touch callback sees them): a surface for the pen. C: R_TOUCH_MODE_NONE

  /// The stage of a touch (`R_TOUCH_*`).
  UITouchPhase = choices(
    Down = 1168,  /// A finger came down. C: R_TOUCH_DOWN
    Move,         /// The touch moved. C: R_TOUCH_MOVE
    Up,           /// The finger was lifted. C: R_TOUCH_UP
    Cancel);      /// The system took the finger away (a gesture of its own, the window lost it): nothing must happen as for a lift. C: R_TOUCH_CANCEL

  /// The stage of a pen (stylus) input (`R_PEN_*`).
  UIPenPhase = choices(
    Down = 1184,  /// The tip touched the screen. C: R_PEN_DOWN
    Move,         /// The pen moves while touching. C: R_PEN_MOVE
    Up,           /// The tip left the screen. C: R_PEN_UP
    Hover,        /// The pen moves near the screen without touching it. C: R_PEN_HOVER
    Leave);       /// The pen went out of reach. C: R_PEN_LEAVE

  /// A pen's barrel button (`R_PEN_BUTTON_*`).
  /// A member's value is its bit number in Raven's flags (a set of them casts to them).
  UIPenButton = choices(
    Barrel = 0,  /// The pen's barrel button. C: R_PEN_BUTTON_BARREL
    Barrel2);    /// The pen's second barrel button. C: R_PEN_BUTTON_BARREL2
  /// A set of `UIPenButton` (Raven's `RPenButton`).
  UIPenButtons = set of UIPenButton;

  /// The stage of a gesture (`R_GESTURE_BEGIN` ..).
  UIGesturePhase = choices(
    Begin = 1200,  /// A second finger came down (a touch screen), or the system recognized a gesture (a trackpad). C: R_GESTURE_BEGIN
    Update,        /// The gesture went on. C: R_GESTURE_UPDATE
    End);          /// Fewer than two fingers remain, or the fingers left the trackpad (RGestureEvent::cancelled: the system took the gesture back). C: R_GESTURE_END

  /// The kind of a gesture (`R_GESTURE_PINCH`, `R_GESTURE_SWIPE`).
  UIGestureKind = choices(
    Pinch = 1216,  /// Two fingers that pinch, turn and move together: scale, rotation and pan. C: R_GESTURE_PINCH
    Swipe);        /// Three or more fingers that move together on a trackpad: only the pan (scale stays 1). By default, a swipe across goes back or forward. C: R_GESTURE_SWIPE

  /// The device a gesture comes from (`R_GESTURE_DEVICE_*`).
  UIGestureDevice = choices(
    Touchscreen = 1232,  /// On the screen: the library recognized the gesture. C: R_GESTURE_DEVICE_TOUCHSCREEN
    Trackpad);           /// On a trackpad: the system recognized the gesture; the fingers are not on the window (x, y is the pointer). C: R_GESTURE_DEVICE_TRACKPAD

  /// A built-in look: a theme and its materials together (`R_LOOK_*`).
  UILook = choices(
    RavenDark = 224,         /// Raven, flat and dense, for tools. The look at start. C: R_LOOK_RAVEN_DARK
    RavenLight,              /// The light variant of `RavenDark`. C: R_LOOK_RAVEN_LIGHT
    RavenGlassDark,          /// Raven in glass: controls are capsules of translucent glass that refract and blur what is behind them, catch the light on their rim and react to the pointer with short animations. Windows get a soft colored background unless they have their own (Rwindow_set_background, Rwindow_set_clear_color). C: R_LOOK_RAVEN_GLASS_DARK
    RavenGlassLight,         /// The light variant of `RavenGlassDark`. C: R_LOOK_RAVEN_GLASS_LIGHT
    RavenHighContrastDark,   /// High contrast, for low vision: pure black and white, yellow (or blue) focus and selection, thick borders, larger text (raven_accessibility.h, Raccessibility_set_high_contrast). C: R_LOOK_RAVEN_HIGH_CONTRAST_DARK
    RavenHighContrastLight,  /// The light variant of `RavenHighContrastDark`. C: R_LOOK_RAVEN_HIGH_CONTRAST_LIGHT
    WindowsDark,             /// Windows 11 (Fluent): its controls, its colors, the accent color the user chose (on Windows), the Segoe UI font when the system has it, and motion without bounce. C: R_LOOK_WINDOWS_DARK
    WindowsLight,            /// The light variant of `WindowsDark`. C: R_LOOK_WINDOWS_LIGHT
    MacosDark,               /// MacOS (Sequoia, Aqua): its controls, its colors, the accent color the user chose (on macOS), the San Francisco font when the system has it, no change under the pointer, and selections in the accent color. C: R_LOOK_MACOS_DARK
    MacosLight,              /// The light variant of `MacosDark`. C: R_LOOK_MACOS_LIGHT
    GnomeDark,               /// GNOME (libadwaita), the desktop of most Linux distributions: flat rounded controls, the accent and the font of the desktop (on Linux). C: R_LOOK_GNOME_DARK
    GnomeLight,              /// The light variant of `GnomeDark`. C: R_LOOK_GNOME_LIGHT
    NativeDark,              /// The look of the platform the application runs on: Windows on Windows, macOS on macOS (macOS Glass from macOS 26 on), GNOME on Linux and the other systems. C: R_LOOK_NATIVE_DARK
    NativeLight,             /// The light variant of `NativeDark`. C: R_LOOK_NATIVE_LIGHT
    MacosGlassDark,          /// MacOS 26 (Tahoe, Liquid Glass): the controls of macOS, larger and rounder, and glass where the system puts it, on what floats above the content: header bars and their buttons, menus, drop-down lists, tooltips, sheets; the knobs of sliders and switches turn into a lens of clear glass while they are held. The content itself (fields, lists, text) stays opaque. The accent color and the font of the system, on macOS. C: R_LOOK_MACOS_GLASS_DARK
    MacosGlassLight);        /// The light variant of `MacosGlassDark`. C: R_LOOK_MACOS_GLASS_LIGHT

  /// A built-in theme (`R_THEME_*`).
  UIThemeKind = choices(
    Dark = 224,          /// Flat, dense themes for tools. C: R_THEME_DARK
    Light,               /// The light variant of `Dark`. C: R_THEME_LIGHT
    GlassDark,           /// Glass themes: controls are capsules of translucent glass that refract and blur what is behind them, catch the light on their rim and react to the pointer with short animations. Windows get a soft colored background unless they have their own (Rwindow_set_background, Rwindow_set_clear_color). C: R_THEME_GLASS_DARK
    GlassLight,          /// The light variant of `GlassDark`. C: R_THEME_GLASS_LIGHT
    HighContrastDark,    /// High contrast, for low vision: pure black and white, yellow (or blue) focus and selection, thick borders, larger text (raven_accessibility.h, Raccessibility_set_high_contrast). C: R_THEME_HIGH_CONTRAST_DARK
    HighContrastLight);  /// The light variant of `HighContrastDark`. C: R_THEME_HIGH_CONTRAST_LIGHT

  /// The surface a widget is drawn with (`R_MATERIAL_*`).
  UIMaterial = choices(
    Solid = 736,   /// Opaque: filled with the colors of the theme. The material of R_THEME_DARK and R_THEME_LIGHT. C: R_MATERIAL_SOLID
    Glass,         /// Clear glass: what is behind stays sharp enough to be recognized, strongly bent at the rim. C: R_MATERIAL_GLASS
    FrostedGlass,  /// Frosted glass: what is behind is blurred into soft colors. The material of the glass themes. C: R_MATERIAL_FROSTED_GLASS
    TintedGlass,   /// Frosted glass colored by the accent color of the theme (or of the widget): for what must stand out. C: R_MATERIAL_TINTED_GLASS
    Default);      /// Not a material: "the one of the theme". Removes the material given to a widget. C: R_MATERIAL_DEFAULT

  /// A theme colour's role (`R_COLOR_*`).
  UIColorRole = choices(
    Window = 256,     /// Window clear color. C: R_COLOR_WINDOW
    Panel,            /// Border background. C: R_COLOR_PANEL
    Border,           /// Border outline, list and input outlines. C: R_COLOR_BORDER
    Text,             /// Text. Inherited by the children of the widget it is set on. C: R_COLOR_TEXT
    TextDisabled,     /// `Text` on a disabled widget. C: R_COLOR_TEXT_DISABLED
    TextPlaceholder,  /// The text placeholder colour. C: R_COLOR_TEXT_PLACEHOLDER
    Accent,           /// Primary buttons, checked boxes, slider fill, progress fill. C: R_COLOR_ACCENT
    AccentHovered,    /// `Accent` while hovered. C: R_COLOR_ACCENT_HOVERED
    AccentPressed,    /// `Accent` while pressed. C: R_COLOR_ACCENT_PRESSED
    AccentText,       /// Text and marks drawn on top of the accent color. C: R_COLOR_ACCENT_TEXT
    Control,          /// Button, combo box, check box background. C: R_COLOR_CONTROL
    ControlHovered,   /// `Control` while hovered. C: R_COLOR_CONTROL_HOVERED
    ControlPressed,   /// `Control` while pressed. C: R_COLOR_CONTROL_PRESSED
    ControlBorder,    /// `Control` as its border. C: R_COLOR_CONTROL_BORDER
    Input,            /// Text input, spin box, list and tree background. C: R_COLOR_INPUT
    Focus,            /// Keyboard focus outline. C: R_COLOR_FOCUS
    Selection,        /// Selected rows and selected text. C: R_COLOR_SELECTION
    RowHovered,       /// The row hovered colour. C: R_COLOR_ROW_HOVERED
    Track,            /// Slider track, progress background, scrollbar track. C: R_COLOR_TRACK
    Handle,           /// Scrollbar thumb, slider handle. C: R_COLOR_HANDLE
    HandleHovered,    /// `Handle` while hovered. C: R_COLOR_HANDLE_HOVERED
    Separator,        /// The separator colour. C: R_COLOR_SEPARATOR
    Header,           /// Menu bar, tab bar, expander header. C: R_COLOR_HEADER
    HeaderHovered,    /// `Header` while hovered. C: R_COLOR_HEADER_HOVERED
    TabActive,        /// Active tab. C: R_COLOR_TAB_ACTIVE
    Popup,            /// Menus, combo box lists. C: R_COLOR_POPUP
    PopupBorder,      /// `Popup` as its border. C: R_COLOR_POPUP_BORDER
    Shadow,           /// The shadow colour. C: R_COLOR_SHADOW
    Tooltip,          /// The tooltip colour. C: R_COLOR_TOOLTIP
    TooltipText,      /// The tooltip text colour. C: R_COLOR_TOOLTIP_TEXT
    Switch,           /// Track of a switch that is on. C: R_COLOR_SWITCH
    Success,          /// What went well, what needs attention, what is wrong or destroys something (markers, badges, classes). C: R_COLOR_SUCCESS
    Warning,          /// The warning colour. C: R_COLOR_WARNING
    Danger,           /// The danger colour. C: R_COLOR_DANGER
    Link,             /// Links of formatted text. C: R_COLOR_LINK
    Code);            /// Background of code in formatted text. C: R_COLOR_CODE

  /// A colour filter over the whole output, for accessibility (`R_COLOR_FILTER_*`).
  UIColorFilter = choices(
    None = 1856,             /// No filter. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_NONE
    Protanopia,              /// Red is weak. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_PROTANOPIA
    Deuteranopia,            /// Green is weak (the most frequent). C: R_COLOR_FILTER_DEUTERANOPIA
    Tritanopia,              /// Blue is weak. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_TRITANOPIA
    Grayscale,               /// Grayscale. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_GRAYSCALE
    Invert,                  /// The colours inverted. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_INVERT
    SimulateProtanopia,      /// Simulations, to see an interface as the color blind see it. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_SIMULATE_PROTANOPIA
    SimulateDeuteranopia,    /// Shows the output as a person with deuteranopia sees it. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_SIMULATE_DEUTERANOPIA
    SimulateTritanopia,      /// Shows the output as a person with tritanopia sees it. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_SIMULATE_TRITANOPIA
    SimulateAchromatopsia);  /// Shows the output as a person with achromatopsia sees it. C: R_COLOR_FILTER_SIMULATE_ACHROMATOPSIA

  /// A theme size's role (`R_METRIC_*`).
  UIMetric = choices(
    FontSize = 320,    /// The font size. C: R_METRIC_FONT_SIZE
    CornerRadius,      /// The corner radius. C: R_METRIC_CORNER_RADIUS
    BorderWidth,       /// The border width. C: R_METRIC_BORDER_WIDTH
    ControlHeight,     /// Height of buttons, inputs, combo boxes, tabs, menu bars. C: R_METRIC_CONTROL_HEIGHT
    PaddingX,          /// Horizontal / vertical padding inside controls. C: R_METRIC_PADDING_X
    PaddingY,          /// The vertical padding. C: R_METRIC_PADDING_Y
    Spacing,           /// Gap between an icon or a check mark and its text. C: R_METRIC_SPACING
    ScrollbarSize,     /// The scrollbar size. C: R_METRIC_SCROLLBAR_SIZE
    RowHeight,         /// Height of list, tree and menu rows. C: R_METRIC_ROW_HEIGHT
    Indent,            /// Indentation per tree level. C: R_METRIC_INDENT
    SplitterSize,      /// The splitter size. C: R_METRIC_SPLITTER_SIZE
    CheckSize,         /// The check size. C: R_METRIC_CHECK_SIZE
    SliderHandleSize,  /// The slider handle size. C: R_METRIC_SLIDER_HANDLE_SIZE
    PopupRadius,       /// Corner radius of menus, drop-down lists and tooltips. C: R_METRIC_POPUP_RADIUS
    GlassFrost,        /// The glass of the theme: each one multiplies what the material gives, 1 = unchanged. Frost (how much is blurred), refraction (how far the rim bends what is behind), saturation (of what is seen through), rim (the light it catches) and shadow (the one it drops). C: R_METRIC_GLASS_FROST
    GlassRefraction,   /// The glass refraction. C: R_METRIC_GLASS_REFRACTION
    GlassSaturation,   /// The glass saturation. C: R_METRIC_GLASS_SATURATION
    GlassRim,          /// The glass rim. C: R_METRIC_GLASS_RIM
    GlassShadow,       /// The glass shadow. C: R_METRIC_GLASS_SHADOW
    BlurRadius);       /// Radius of the blur of a BackgroundBlur that was not given one. C: R_METRIC_BLUR_RADIUS

  /// A font's style (`R_FONT_*`).
  UIFontStyle = choices(
    Regular = 1056,  /// Regular. C: R_FONT_REGULAR
    Bold,            /// Bold. C: R_FONT_BOLD
    Italic,          /// Italic. C: R_FONT_ITALIC
    BoldItalic);     /// Bold italic. C: R_FONT_BOLD_ITALIC

  /// How a texture is sampled when scaled (`R_FILTER_*`).
  UIFilter = choices(
    Linear = 704,  /// Linear smoothing. C: R_FILTER_LINEAR
    Nearest,       /// No smoothing: keeps pixel art sharp. C: R_FILTER_NEAREST
    Mipmap);       /// Smooth, with mipmaps: an image shown much smaller than its size stays clean instead of shimmering, for a third more GPU memory. The default of the textures made from image files (Rtexture_create...). Backends without mipmaps treat it as R_FILTER_LINEAR. C: R_FILTER_MIPMAP

  /// A texture's pixel format (`R_TEXTURE_*`).
  UITextureFormat = choices(
    RGBA8 = 720,  /// 4 bytes per pixel: R, G, B, A. C: R_TEXTURE_RGBA8
    Alpha8);      /// 1 byte per pixel, sampled as (1, 1, 1, value). Used by the glyph atlas. C: R_TEXTURE_ALPHA8

  /// The kind of a widget (`R_WIDGET_*`).
  UIWidgetKind = choices(
    VBox = 512,      /// Stacks children top to bottom. C: R_WIDGET_VBOX
    HBox,            /// Stacks children left to right. C: R_WIDGET_HBOX
    Grid,            /// Rows and columns with spans and fill coefficients. C: R_WIDGET_GRID
    UniformGrid,     /// Grid whose cells all have the same size. C: R_WIDGET_UNIFORM_GRID
    Overlay,         /// Draws children on top of each other. C: R_WIDGET_OVERLAY
    Border,          /// One child with a background, an outline and inner padding. C: R_WIDGET_BORDER
    SizeBox,         /// One child with size constraints or a fixed aspect ratio. C: R_WIDGET_SIZE_BOX
    Spacer,          /// Empty space. C: R_WIDGET_SPACER
    ScrollBox,       /// Scrollable stack of children. C: R_WIDGET_SCROLL_BOX
    Splitter,        /// Children separated by draggable handles. C: R_WIDGET_SPLITTER
    WrapBox,         /// Flows children and wraps to the next line. C: R_WIDGET_WRAP_BOX
    Canvas,          /// Children placed with anchors and offsets. C: R_WIDGET_CANVAS
    Switcher,        /// Shows one child at a time. C: R_WIDGET_SWITCHER
    TabView,         /// Tab bar + one page per child. C: R_WIDGET_TAB_VIEW
    Expander,        /// Collapsible header + one child. C: R_WIDGET_EXPANDER
    Label,           /// ---- controls (raven_controls.h) ----. C: R_WIDGET_LABEL
    Button,          /// A button. C: R_WIDGET_BUTTON
    CheckBox,        /// A check box. C: R_WIDGET_CHECKBOX
    Slider,          /// A slider. C: R_WIDGET_SLIDER
    ProgressBar,     /// A progress bar. C: R_WIDGET_PROGRESSBAR
    Image,           /// An image. C: R_WIDGET_IMAGE
    TextInput,       /// A text input. C: R_WIDGET_TEXT_INPUT
    SpinBox,         /// A spin box. C: R_WIDGET_SPIN_BOX
    ComboBox,        /// A combo box. C: R_WIDGET_COMBO_BOX
    Separator,       /// A separator. C: R_WIDGET_SEPARATOR
    ListView,        /// A list view. C: R_WIDGET_LIST_VIEW
    TreeView,        /// A tree view. C: R_WIDGET_TREE_VIEW
    MenuBar,         /// A menu bar. C: R_WIDGET_MENU_BAR
    Menu,            /// A menu. C: R_WIDGET_MENU
    MenuItem,        /// A menu item. C: R_WIDGET_MENU_ITEM
    Viewport,        /// Area showing content rendered by the application. C: R_WIDGET_VIEWPORT
    Custom,          /// Widget painted and measured by application callbacks. C: R_WIDGET_CUSTOM
    TextEditor,      /// Multi-line text editor. C: R_WIDGET_TEXT_EDITOR
    HeaderBar,       /// Title bar of a window with a custom header, holding any widget. C: R_WIDGET_HEADER_BAR
    DockArea,        /// Panels docked side by side or behind tabs, that the user rearranges. C: R_WIDGET_DOCK_AREA
    Island,          /// A capsule that unfolds into a panel, at the top of a window. C: R_WIDGET_ISLAND
    FileBrowser,     /// Explorer of the files of the computer. C: R_WIDGET_FILE_BROWSER
    BackgroundBlur,  /// One child over a blurred view of what is behind it. C: R_WIDGET_BACKGROUND_BLUR
    ColorPicker,     /// Chooses a color: hue, saturation, value, opacity, by hand or by numbers. C: R_WIDGET_COLOR_PICKER
    Timeline,        /// Tracks of clips and keys along a time ruler. C: R_WIDGET_TIMELINE
    NodeGraph,       /// Nodes linked by wires, on a canvas that pans and zooms. C: R_WIDGET_NODE_GRAPH
    TileView,        /// Grid of tiles (an icon over a name), virtualized. C: R_WIDGET_TILE_VIEW
    BlockEditor,     /// Blocks that snap into each other, in the style of Scratch. C: R_WIDGET_BLOCK_EDITOR
    Table,           /// Rows of cells under columns that can be resized and sorted, virtualized. C: R_WIDGET_TABLE
    DatePicker,      /// A date, chosen in a calendar that drops down. C: R_WIDGET_DATE_PICKER
    TimePicker,      /// A time of the day: hours, minutes, optionally seconds. C: R_WIDGET_TIME_PICKER
    Toast,           /// A short message that rises for a few seconds, with an optional action ("Undo"). C: R_WIDGET_TOAST
    Breadcrumb,      /// The path to the current place: links separated by chevrons. C: R_WIDGET_BREADCRUMB
    Rating,          /// A score shown and chosen with stars. C: R_WIDGET_RATING
    Pagination,      /// Page numbers with previous and next. C: R_WIDGET_PAGINATION
    Plot,            /// Curves of X / Y data: legend, line styles, markers, log axes, a second X and Y axis, pan and zoom. C: R_WIDGET_PLOT
    PDFView,         /// The pages of a PDF document, scrolled and zoomed (drawn by PDFium, loaded at run time). C: R_WIDGET_PDF_VIEW
    Chart,           /// The charts of dashboards: pie, donut, gauge, heatmap, sparkline (RChartKind). C: R_WIDGET_CHART
    MapView,         /// A map of slippy-map tiles given by the application (or read from files): panned, zoomed, with markers. C: R_WIDGET_MAP_VIEW
    Carousel);       /// Pages shown one at a time and swiped (a page view), with dots and arrows. C: R_WIDGET_CAROUSEL
  /// A set of `UIWidgetKind` (the kinds a widget type views: `UIWidget.Kinds`).
  UIWidgetKinds = set of UIWidgetKind;

  /// How a widget lines up across its slot (`R_HALIGN_*`).
  UIHAlign = choices(
    Fill = 576,  /// Fills the slot across. C: R_HALIGN_FILL
    Left,        /// At the left. C: R_HALIGN_LEFT
    Center,      /// Centred across the slot. C: R_HALIGN_CENTER
    Right);      /// At the right. C: R_HALIGN_RIGHT

  /// How a widget lines up down its slot (`R_VALIGN_*`).
  UIVAlign = choices(
    Fill = 592,  /// Fills the slot down. C: R_VALIGN_FILL
    Top,         /// At the top. C: R_VALIGN_TOP
    Center,      /// Centred down the slot. C: R_VALIGN_CENTER
    Bottom);     /// At the bottom. C: R_VALIGN_BOTTOM

  /// Whether a widget shows and takes room (`R_VISIBLE`, `R_HIDDEN`, `R_COLLAPSED`).
  UIVisibility = choices(
    Visible = 608,  /// Drawn and laid out. C: R_VISIBLE
    Hidden,         /// Not drawn, but still takes its space in the layout. C: R_HIDDEN
    Collapsed);     /// Not drawn and takes no space. C: R_COLLAPSED

  /// A direction of layout (`R_HORIZONTAL`, `R_VERTICAL`).
  UIOrientation = choices(
    Horizontal = 624,  /// Horizontal. C: R_HORIZONTAL
    Vertical);         /// Vertical. C: R_VERTICAL

  /// How a widget's content changes over (`R_TRANSITION_*`).
  UITransition = choices(
    None = 768,   /// No transition. C: R_TRANSITION_NONE
    Fade,         /// Becomes opaque. C: R_TRANSITION_FADE
    Pop,          /// Grows from a smaller size and bounces a little past its own. C: R_TRANSITION_POP
    Zoom,         /// Shrinks from a larger size. C: R_TRANSITION_ZOOM
    FlyUp,        /// Flies in from below / above / the right / the left, and settles with a bounce. C: R_TRANSITION_FLY_UP
    FlyDown,      /// The new content flies in downwards. C: R_TRANSITION_FLY_DOWN
    FlyLeft,      /// The new content flies in to the left. C: R_TRANSITION_FLY_LEFT
    FlyRight,     /// The new content flies in to the right. C: R_TRANSITION_FLY_RIGHT
    Drop,         /// Falls from above, squashes on landing and wobbles. C: R_TRANSITION_DROP
    SlideLeft,    /// Short slide from the right / from the left, without bounce: pages that replace one another. C: R_TRANSITION_SLIDE_LEFT
    SlideRight);  /// The new content slides in to the right. C: R_TRANSITION_SLIDE_RIGHT

  /// A background blur's style (`R_BLUR_*`).
  UIBlurStyle = choices(
    Plain = 1088,  /// What is behind, out of focus, and nothing else (a Gaussian blur). C: R_BLUR_PLAIN
    Frosted,       /// Frosted: blurred, its colors a little stronger, under a veil of the panel color of the theme, a fine grain and a hairline. The default. C: R_BLUR_FROSTED
    Glass,         /// Glass: a slab that bends what is behind at its rim and catches the light, as the glass materials do (RMaterial); the radius says how frosted it is. C: R_BLUR_GLASS
    Native);       /// Native: the widget opens the window there, and what shows is what the OS puts behind the window (Rwindow_set_backdrop: the blurred desktop, acrylic, mica), under a light veil. It needs a window created with R_WINDOW_TRANSPARENT that the OS could make see-through; anywhere else it is drawn as R_BLUR_FROSTED. The radius is the one of the OS. C: R_BLUR_NATIVE

  /// The layout direction: left to right or right to left (`R_DIRECTION_*`).
  UIDirection = choices(
    Inherit = 0,  /// A widget: the direction of its parent (the default). C: R_DIRECTION_INHERIT
    LTR = 1824,   /// Left to right. C: R_DIRECTION_LTR
    RTL,          /// Right to left. C: R_DIRECTION_RTL
    Auto);        /// The windows: the direction of the language. C: R_DIRECTION_AUTO

  /// A toast's kind (`R_TOAST_INFO` ..).
  UIToastKind = choices(
    Info = 1248,  /// A neutral message (the accent of the theme). C: R_TOAST_INFO
    Success,      /// A success toast. C: R_TOAST_SUCCESS
    Warning,      /// A warning toast. C: R_TOAST_WARNING
    Error);       /// An error toast. C: R_TOAST_ERROR

  /// How a new toast meets the shown one (`R_TOAST_REPLACE` ..).
  UIToastQueue = choices(
    Replace = 1280,  /// The new message takes the place of the one shown (the default). C: R_TOAST_REPLACE
    Sequence,        /// The messages are shown one after the other, each for its own time. C: R_TOAST_SEQUENCE
    Stack);          /// Up to Rtoast_set_max_visible messages are shown at once, one above the other; the others wait. C: R_TOAST_STACK

  /// A button's style (`R_BUTTON_*`).
  UIButtonStyle = choices(
    Default = 656,  /// Filled with R_COLOR_CONTROL. C: R_BUTTON_DEFAULT
    Primary,        /// Filled with R_COLOR_ACCENT. C: R_BUTTON_PRIMARY
    Flat);          /// No background until hovered (toolbars). C: R_BUTTON_FLAT

  /// A check box's style (`R_CHECKBOX_*`).
  UICheckStyle = choices(
    Check = 672,  /// A check box. C: R_CHECKBOX_CHECK
    Radio,        /// Round mark. Checking one unchecks the other radio boxes of the same parent. C: R_CHECKBOX_RADIO
    Switch);      /// On / off switch. C: R_CHECKBOX_SWITCH

  /// How content fills its box (`R_STRETCH_*`).
  UIStretch = choices(
    Fill = 688,  /// Stretches the image to the widget, ignoring its aspect ratio. C: R_STRETCH_FILL
    Fit,         /// Largest size that fits entirely, keeping the aspect ratio. C: R_STRETCH_FIT
    Cover,       /// Smallest size that covers the widget, keeping the aspect ratio (cropped). C: R_STRETCH_COVER
    None);       /// Original size, centered. C: R_STRETCH_NONE

  /// A plot axis (`R_PLOT_X` ..).
  UIAxis = choices(
    X = 1312,  /// The horizontal axis under the data. C: R_PLOT_X
    Y,         /// The vertical axis on the left. C: R_PLOT_Y
    X2,        /// A second horizontal axis, over the data: shown when a series or a drag line uses it. C: R_PLOT_X2
    Y2);       /// A second vertical axis, on the right: shown when a series or a drag line uses it. C: R_PLOT_Y2

  /// A plot axis's scale (`R_PLOT_SCALE_*`).
  UIAxisScale = choices(
    Linear = 1328,  /// A linear scale. C: R_PLOT_SCALE_LINEAR
    Log,            /// Powers of ten at even distances; only values above zero are shown. C: R_PLOT_SCALE_LOG
    Symlog);        /// Symmetric logarithm: linear between -t and t (Rplot_set_axis_linear_threshold, 1 by default), logarithmic beyond on both sides: shows zero and the negative values a logarithm cannot. C: R_PLOT_SCALE_SYMLOG

  /// A plot line's style (`R_PLOT_LINE_*`).
  UILineStyle = choices(
    Solid = 1344,  /// Solid lines. C: R_PLOT_LINE_SOLID
    Dashed,        /// Dashed lines. C: R_PLOT_LINE_DASHED
    Dotted,        /// Dotted lines. C: R_PLOT_LINE_DOTTED
    DashDot,       /// Dash-dot lines. C: R_PLOT_LINE_DASH_DOT
    None);         /// No line: only the markers (a scatter plot). C: R_PLOT_LINE_NONE

  /// A plot point's marker (`R_PLOT_MARKER_*`).
  UIMarkerShape = choices(
    None = 1360,   /// No marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_NONE
    Circle,        /// A circle marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_CIRCLE
    Square,        /// A square marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_SQUARE
    Diamond,       /// A diamond marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_DIAMOND
    TriangleUp,    /// A triangle up marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_TRIANGLE_UP
    TriangleDown,  /// A triangle down marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_TRIANGLE_DOWN
    Cross,         /// A cross marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_CROSS
    Plus,          /// A plus marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_PLUS
    Asterisk);     /// An asterisk marker. C: R_PLOT_MARKER_ASTERISK

  /// Where a plot's legend goes (`R_PLOT_LEGEND_*`).
  UILegendPlace = choices(
    Hidden = 1376,  /// No legend. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_HIDDEN
    TopLeft,        /// At the top left. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_TOP_LEFT
    Top,            /// At the top. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_TOP
    TopRight,       /// At the top right. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_TOP_RIGHT
    Right,          /// At the right. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_RIGHT
    BottomRight,    /// At the bottom right. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_BOTTOM_RIGHT
    Bottom,         /// At the bottom. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_BOTTOM
    BottomLeft,     /// At the bottom left. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_BOTTOM_LEFT
    Left,           /// At the left. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_LEFT
    Outside);       /// To the right of the data, outside it. C: R_PLOT_LEGEND_OUTSIDE

  /// How a PDF page fits its view (`R_PDF_FIT_*`).
  UIPDFFit = choices(
    Width = 1472,  /// The widest page fills the width of the view (default). C: R_PDF_FIT_WIDTH
    Page,          /// The largest page fits whole in the view. C: R_PDF_FIT_PAGE
    None);         /// The zoom of Rpdf_view_set_zoom; zooming with the wheel or the keys switches to it. C: R_PDF_FIT_NONE

  /// A PDF view's state (`R_PDF_EMPTY` ..).
  UIPDFStatus = choices(
    Empty = 1488,   /// No document. C: R_PDF_EMPTY
    Loaded,         /// A document is shown. C: R_PDF_LOADED
    NeedsPassword,  /// The document needs a password, or the one given is wrong: load it again with one. C: R_PDF_NEEDS_PASSWORD
    Error,          /// The file could not be read, or is not a PDF document. C: R_PDF_ERROR
    Unavailable);   /// The PDFium library was not found (see Rpdf_is_available). C: R_PDF_UNAVAILABLE

  /// A font PDF drawing writes with (`R_PDF_FONT_*`).
  UIPDFFont = choices(
    Sans = 0,  /// Roboto, the font of the interface of Raven. C: R_PDF_FONT_SANS
    Mono);     /// Roboto Mono. C: R_PDF_FONT_MONO

  /// How a PDF shape is painted (`R_PDF_FILL`, `R_PDF_STROKE`).
  /// A member's value is its bit number in Raven's flags (a set of them casts to them).
  UIPDFPaint = choices(
    Fill = 0,  /// Filled with the fill color. C: R_PDF_FILL
    Stroke);   /// Outlined with the stroke color and the line width. C: R_PDF_STROKE
  /// A set of `UIPDFPaint` (Raven's `RPdfPaint`).
  UIPDFPaints = set of UIPDFPaint;

  /// A PDF text style (`R_PDF_TEXT_*`).
  /// A member's value is its bit number in Raven's flags (a set of them casts to them).
  UIPDFText = choices(
    Bold = 0,    /// Bold. C: R_PDF_TEXT_BOLD
    Italic,      /// Italic. C: R_PDF_TEXT_ITALIC
    Underline);  /// Underline. C: R_PDF_TEXT_UNDERLINE
  /// A set of `UIPDFText` (Raven's `RPdfTextStyle`).
  UIPDFTexts = set of UIPDFText;

  /// A printing option (`R_PDF_PRINT_*`).
  /// A member's value is its bit number in Raven's flags (a set of them casts to them).
  UIPrintFlag = choices(
    NoDialog = 0);  /// No dialog: printed at once on the printer named, else the default one. C: R_PDF_PRINT_NO_DIALOG
  /// A set of `UIPrintFlag` (Raven's `RPdfPrintFlags`).
  UIPrintFlags = set of UIPrintFlag;

  /// A map tile's state (`R_MAP_TILE_*`).
  UITileState = choices(
    None = 1536,  /// Not in the view's cache: never asked for, no longer wanted, or evicted. C: R_MAP_TILE_NONE
    Pending,      /// Asked for (the tile callback was called, or the file is being read): waiting for its pixels. C: R_MAP_TILE_PENDING
    Loaded,       /// Its pixels are in the cache. C: R_MAP_TILE_LOADED
    Failed);      /// The application said it has none (Rmap_view_set_tile_failed), or its file could not be read. C: R_MAP_TILE_FAILED

  /// A chart's kind (`R_CHART_*`).
  UIChartKind = choices(
    Pie = 1424,  /// Slices of a whole, as parts of a disc (the default). C: R_CHART_PIE
    Donut,       /// Slices of a whole, as parts of a ring; its middle shows the total, or the slice under the pointer. C: R_CHART_DONUT
    Gauge,       /// One value within a range, on an arc; bands color parts of the range. C: R_CHART_GAUGE
    Heatmap,     /// A grid of values, each cell colored from the low color to the high one. C: R_CHART_HEATMAP
    Sparkline);  /// A small line of values without axes, to sit in a tile or a cell of a table. C: R_CHART_SPARKLINE

  /// A text editor's built-in highlighting (`R_SYNTAX_*`).
  UISyntax = choices(
    None = 832,  /// No highlighting. C: R_SYNTAX_NONE
    XML,         /// XML highlighting. C: R_SYNTAX_XML
    C);          /// C highlighting. C: R_SYNTAX_C

  /// A syntax language's option (`R_LANGUAGE_*`).
  /// A member's value is its bit number in Raven's flags (a set of them casts to them).
  UILanguageFlag = choices(
    Markup = 0,      /// Tags and attributes instead of code: XML, HTML. The words and the comments of the description are not used. C: R_LANGUAGE_MARKUP
    StyleSheet,      /// Selectors, properties and values: CSS. C: R_LANGUAGE_STYLE_SHEET
    NestedComments,  /// A block comment may hold another one (Rust). C: R_LANGUAGE_NESTED_COMMENTS
    CharLiterals,    /// Between single quotes there is one character; any other single quote is not a text (C, Java, Rust). C: R_LANGUAGE_CHAR_LITERALS
    IndentOnColon,   /// A line that ends with ':' indents the next one (Python). C: R_LANGUAGE_INDENT_ON_COLON
    IgnoreCase,      /// The words of the language are recognized whatever their case. C: R_LANGUAGE_IGNORE_CASE
    Embeds,          /// Markup that holds JavaScript in script elements and CSS in style elements (HTML). C: R_LANGUAGE_EMBEDS
    FormattedText);  /// Formatted text written in Markdown: titles, strong and emphasized text, code, links, lists. The editor shows the text as it is written, marks included, with strong text in bold, emphasized text in italic and titles in bold: what will be formatted is seen while typing. C: R_LANGUAGE_FORMATTED_TEXT
  /// A set of `UILanguageFlag` (Raven's `RLanguageFlags`).
  UILanguageFlags = set of UILanguageFlag;

  /// A highlighted token's kind (`R_TOKEN_*`).
  UITokenKind = choices(
    Text = 928,   /// Plain text. C: R_TOKEN_TEXT
    Comment,      /// A comment. C: R_TOKEN_COMMENT
    String,       /// A string. C: R_TOKEN_STRING
    Number,       /// A number. C: R_TOKEN_NUMBER
    Keyword,      /// A keyword. C: R_TOKEN_KEYWORD
    Type,         /// A type, or a name that is always there. C: R_TOKEN_TYPE
    Function,     /// A name followed by an opening parenthesis. C: R_TOKEN_FUNCTION
    Tag,          /// The name of an element, in markup and in the selectors of a style sheet. C: R_TOKEN_TAG
    Attribute,    /// The name of an attribute (markup), of a class or of a property (style sheets), of a key (JSON). C: R_TOKEN_ATTRIBUTE
    Punctuation,  /// Punctuation. C: R_TOKEN_PUNCTUATION
    Directive,    /// A line for the preprocessor, an annotation, a declaration of a document. C: R_TOKEN_DIRECTIVE
    Heading,      /// Formatted text (the Markdown language): a title, strong text, emphasized text, a link. C: R_TOKEN_HEADING
    Strong,       /// Strong (bold) text. C: R_TOKEN_STRONG
    Emphasis,     /// Emphasized (italic) text. C: R_TOKEN_EMPHASIS
    Link);        /// A link. C: R_TOKEN_LINK

  /// A text editor line mark's kind (`R_MARKER_*`).
  UIMarkKind = choices(
    Error = 848,  /// An error mark. C: R_MARKER_ERROR
    Warning,      /// A warning mark. C: R_MARKER_WARNING
    Info);        /// An info mark. C: R_MARKER_INFO

  /// A header bar's window button (`R_HEADER_*`).
  /// A member's value is its bit number in Raven's flags (a set of them casts to them).
  UIHeaderButton = choices(
    Close = 0,  /// The close button. C: R_HEADER_CLOSE
    Minimize,   /// The minimize button. C: R_HEADER_MINIMIZE
    Maximize);  /// The maximize button. C: R_HEADER_MAXIMIZE
  /// A set of `UIHeaderButton` (Raven's `RHeaderButtons`).
  UIHeaderButtons = set of UIHeaderButton;

  /// The state of a taskbar progress (`R_TASKBAR_PROGRESS_*`).
  UITaskbarProgress = choices(
    None = 1952,     /// No progress shown. C: R_TASKBAR_PROGRESS_NONE
    Normal,          /// Progress shown as it goes. C: R_TASKBAR_PROGRESS_NORMAL
    Paused,          /// Shown as paused (yellow on Windows). C: R_TASKBAR_PROGRESS_PAUSED
    Error,           /// Shown as failed (red on Windows). C: R_TASKBAR_PROGRESS_ERROR
    Indeterminate);  /// Something goes on, without knowing how far it is. C: R_TASKBAR_PROGRESS_INDETERMINATE

  /// Where a docked panel goes (`R_DOCK_*`).
  UIDockSide = choices(
    Left = 864,  /// The left side. C: R_DOCK_LEFT
    Right,       /// The right side. C: R_DOCK_RIGHT
    Top,         /// The top side. C: R_DOCK_TOP
    Bottom,      /// The bottom side. C: R_DOCK_BOTTOM
    Tab);        /// Behind the same tabs as the other panel. C: R_DOCK_TAB

  /// Where an undocked panel floats (`R_DOCK_FLOAT_*`).
  UIDockFloat = choices(
    Window = 0,  /// In a window of its own. C: R_DOCK_FLOAT_WINDOW
    InWindow);   /// Inside the window. C: R_DOCK_FLOAT_IN_WINDOW

  /// A node graph's or timeline's visual preset (`R_PRESET_*`).
  UIPreset = choices(
    Auto = 1296,  /// The look of the theme of the window: its platform, dark or light. C: R_PRESET_AUTO
    Modern,       /// Cards with soft shadows, few lines (follows dark or light). C: R_PRESET_MODERN
    Blueprint,    /// Headers in gradients, a grid of lines, thick links that glow; pins of the type "exec" are arrows. C: R_PRESET_BLUEPRINT
    Blender,      /// Compact nodes, flat headers in muted colors, thin links. C: R_PRESET_BLENDER
    Neon);        /// Almost black, outlines and links of light. C: R_PRESET_NEON

  /// A timeline item's kind (`R_TIMELINE_*`).
  UITimelineItemKind = choices(
    None = 1120,  /// No item. C: R_TIMELINE_NONE
    Clip,         /// A clip. C: R_TIMELINE_CLIP
    Key,          /// A key. C: R_TIMELINE_KEY
    Marker);      /// A marker. C: R_TIMELINE_MARKER

  /// A block editor block's shape (`R_BLOCK_STATEMENT` ..).
  UIBlockShape = choices(
    Statement = 1792,  /// A step: snaps under another one, others snap under it. C: R_BLOCK_STATEMENT
    Hat,               /// Starts a script ("when the game starts"): nothing goes above it. C: R_BLOCK_HAT
    Cap,               /// Ends a script ("stop"): nothing goes under it. C: R_BLOCK_CAP
    C,                 /// Wraps stacks in its mouths ("repeat", "if ... else"). C: R_BLOCK_C
    Reporter,          /// A rounded value that goes into a slot. C: R_BLOCK_REPORTER
    Boolean);          /// A hexagonal condition that goes into a %b slot (or a %r one). C: R_BLOCK_BOOLEAN

  /// Where a block joins another (`R_BLOCK_NEXT` ..).
  UIBlockPart = choices(
